   "source": [
    "# Phase 6A: AI4I 2020 Predictive Maintenance Preprocessing Pipeline\n",
    "## Project: Adaptive Learning for Cloud Security and Predictive Maintenance\n",
    "\n",
    "### Objective:\n",
    "Preprocess the **AI4I 2020 Predictive Maintenance Dataset** for machine failure prediction. This notebook imports the reusable logic from `src/data_processing/maintenance_preprocessing.py`, performing stratified train/test splitting, identifier drops, one-hot encoding for quality `Type`, scaling sensor features, and saving the pipeline to `models/maintenance/preprocessing_pipeline.joblib`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import os\n",
    "import sys\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "\n",
    "# Ensure path to src is available\n",
    "PROJECT_ROOT = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))) if '__file__' in locals() else os.path.abspath('..')\n",
    "sys.path.append(os.path.join(PROJECT_ROOT, 'src'))\n",
    "\n",
    "from data_processing.maintenance_preprocessing import preprocess_ai4i_2020\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Module import successful!\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--- \n",
    "## 1. Rationale for Preprocessing Decisions\n",
    "\n",
    "### A. Identifier & Failure Mode Drops (`UDI`, `Product ID`, `TWF`, `HDF`, `PWF`, `OSF`, `RNF`):\n",
    "- `UDI` (row index) and `Product ID` (serial string) carry zero operational signal. Leaving them in would cause spurious overfitting.\n",
    "- `TWF`, `HDF`, `PWF`, `OSF`, `RNF` are specific failure mode indicators. Including them as input features would directly leak the `Machine failure` target state. Thus, they are dropped from input features.\n",
    "\n",
    "### B. Categorical Encoding (`Type`):\n",
    "- `Type` represents product quality variant (`L`, `M`, `H`). `OneHotEncoder(handle_unknown='ignore', sparse_output=False)` creates binary features (`Type_L`, `Type_M`, `Type_H`).\n",
    "\n",
    "### C. Sensor Feature Scaling (`StandardScaler`):\n",
    "- Operational sensors (`Air temp [K]`, `Process temp [K]`, `Rotational speed [rpm]`, `Torque [Nm]`, `Tool wear [min]`) have different units and magnitudes. `StandardScaler` standardizes features to zero mean ($\mu=0$) and unit variance ($\sigma=1$).\n",
    "\n",
    "### D. Stratified Train/Test Split (75/25):\n",
    "- Given the severe class imbalance (~7.7% failure rate), a stratified train/test split ensures that both training and test sets maintain the exact same 92.3% vs 7.7% target proportion."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--- \n",
    "## 2. Execute Maintenance Preprocessing"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "results = preprocess_ai4i_2020()\n",
    "\n",
    "X_train = results['X_train']\n",
    "X_test = results['X_test']\n",
    "y_train = results['y_train']\n",
    "y_test = results['y_test']\n",
    "pipeline_path = results['pipeline_path']"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--- \n",
    "## 3. Class Imbalance Ratio & Dataset Shapes Inspection"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(\"=== PROCESSED MAINTENANCE DATASET SHAPES ===\")\n",
    "print(f\"X_train shape               : {X_train.shape}\")\n",
    "print(f\"X_test shape                : {X_test.shape}\")\n",
    "print(f\"y_train shape               : {y_train.shape}\")\n",
    "print(f\"y_test shape                : {y_test.shape}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\n=== CLASS IMBALANCE RATIO ===\")\n",
    "print(f\"Healthy (0) Count           : {results['healthy_count']}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Failure (1) Count           : {results['failure_count']}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Imbalance Ratio             : {results['imbalance_ratio']:.2f}:1\")\n",
    "print(f\"Failure Percentage          : {(results['failure_count']/ (results['healthy_count']+results['failure_count']))*100:.2f}%\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"\\nSaved Pipeline Path         : {pipeline_path}\")"
   ]
  }
